{"data": [{"author_id": "68746721", "created_at": "2026-10-31T20:25:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116627718347591988"], "id": "2116627718347591988", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 44, "impression_count": 6795, "like_count": 138, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 22, "retweet_count": 13}, "text": "Dopamine does not spike highest for guaranteed rewards. It spikes highest at reward prediction error. If you want to have fun in life, you should stop avoiding risk and uncertainty.", "url": "https://x.com/fchollet/status/2116627718347591988"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-31T20:19:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116626131906334784"], "id": "2116626131906334784", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 10005, "like_count": 51, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 11, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "If you thought this past week was packed with market-moving news, wait until you see what lies ahead.\nTech earnings, divergence, and central bank developments dominated over the last five days, even as resilient US growth data provided an underlying buffer.\nLooking forward, the", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116626131906334784"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-31T18:26:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116597746992025965"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/thebestqueenx/…", "end": 44, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/thebestqueenx/status/2116236389587259544", "start": 21, "url": "https://t.co/KES9mkmpxU"}]}, "id": "2116597746992025965", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 1857, "like_count": 18, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116236389587259544", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I hate it but also 💯 https://t.co/KES9mkmpxU", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2116597746992025965"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-10-31T18:08:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116593148076138557"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/sarahlicity/st…", "end": 33, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/sarahlicity/status/2115896869943406811", "start": 10, "url": "https://t.co/2s9tz0Qvla"}]}, "id": "2116593148076138557", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1228, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115896869943406811", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "&lt;3 RIP https://t.co/2s9tz0Qvla", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2116593148076138557"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-31T16:11:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116563633216122955"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 213, "start": 205, "tag": "economy"}, {"end": 223, "start": 214, "tag": "marklets"}, {"end": 227, "start": 224, "tag": "ai"}, {"end": 251, "start": 228, "tag": "artificialintelligence"}], "mentions": [{"end": 256, "id": "3108351", "start": 252, "username": "WSJ"}, {"end": 260, "id": "18949452", "start": 257, "username": "FT"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/dcJc51iRwS", "end": 284, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116563633216122955/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116561705509470209", "start": 261, "url": "https://t.co/dcJc51iRwS"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/dcJc51iRwS", "end": 284, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116563633216122955/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116561784622518272", "start": 261, "url": "https://t.co/dcJc51iRwS"}]}, "id": "2116563633216122955", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 16548, "like_count": 56, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 19, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "Narrative following the price action?\nLots of downbeat AI coverage in the media today, including this from the FT and WSJ.\nPredictable given the tape ... but will this sudden pivot to pessimism overshoot?\n#economy #marklets #ai #artificialintelligence @wsj @ft https://t.co/dcJc51iRwS", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116563633216122955"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-31T15:42:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116556346086531197"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/99WWwKVQvK", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116556346086531197/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116556207359950848", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/99WWwKVQvK"}]}, "id": "2116556346086531197", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 12, "impression_count": 26359, "like_count": 174, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 62, "retweet_count": 17}, "text": "Christine Lagarde announced this week that she will step down as President of the European Central Bank.\nCount me among the many who have greatly admired her inspiring tenure, not just at the ECB, but at the IMF before that.\nAn extraordinary leader and visionary who secures https://t.co/99WWwKVQvK", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116556346086531197"}, {"author_id": "321536046", "created_at": "2026-10-31T15:00:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116545865162633326"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "BEA Regional Fact Sheet about personal income, gross domestic product (GDP), personal consumption expenditures (PCE), and foreign direct investment. To view your customized fact sheet, select an area type. State BEARFACTS are based on the state estimates published on September 30, 2026 for GDP, personal income, and PCE by state. County BEARFACTS are based on the county estimates published on February 5, 2026 for GDP and personal", "display_url": "Bea.gov/BEARFacts", "end": 261, "expanded_url": "https://Bea.gov/BEARFacts", "start": 238, "status": 200, "title": "BEA: BEARFACTS", "unwound_url": "https://apps.bea.gov/regional/bearfacts/", "url": "https://t.co/coTEQP5D5J"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/JQAAbYdnpT", "end": 285, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/BEA_News/status/2116545865162633326/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116545850784575489", "start": 262, "url": "https://t.co/JQAAbYdnpT"}]}, "id": "2116545865162633326", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 687, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Don’t be scared to tackle economic data! BEARFacts—BEA Regional Facts—makes it easy to find information for all 50 states and D.C. Consumer spending data is now available, along with GDP, personal income, and foreign direct investment. \n\nhttps://t.co/coTEQP5D5J https://t.co/JQAAbYdnpT", "url": "https://x.com/BEA_News/status/2116545865162633326"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-31T14:25:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116537058433081669"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "About 56 billion people died before Halloween 1926. Where are they?", "display_url": "ghost-census.netlify.app", "end": 276, "expanded_url": "https://ghost-census.netlify.app/", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116537069929635840/DFfolfiV?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116537069929635840/DFfolfiV?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 253, "status": 200, "title": "The Ghost Census", "unwound_url": "https://ghost-census.netlify.app/", "url": "https://t.co/pOGW5aUa2b"}]}, "id": "2116537058433081669", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 35, "impression_count": 15822, "like_count": 189, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 87, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "For Halloween, I asked Opus 5.5 to suggest a spooky project based on my existing work, and it came up with the idea of the ghost census. Pick a location and see how many people died within a 100 meters of it through all of history up to a century ago.  https://t.co/pOGW5aUa2b", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116537058433081669"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-31T13:43:54.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116526579232702587"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 90, "id": "18856867", "start": 80, "username": "zerohedge"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/grJAs02RCe", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116526579232702587/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116526576426708992", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/grJAs02RCe"}]}, "id": "2116526579232702587", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 20, "impression_count": 19898, "like_count": 83, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 28, "retweet_count": 15}, "text": "Dispersion in tech credit:\nThe widening CDS spreads detailed in this table (H/T @zerohedge via LS) illustrates how markets are differentiating across names, notwithstanding the broader macro derisking in the AI trade.\nThe data also points to marlwt opportunities, outright and via https://t.co/grJAs02RCe", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116526579232702587"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-31T13:43:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116526543346483419"], "id": "2116526543346483419", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 73, "impression_count": 25552, "like_count": 457, "quote_count": 26, "reply_count": 234, "retweet_count": 29}, "text": "The market for software migration from legacy systems has been limited to $30B a year or so because migration is very expensive and maintenance is easier. Talking to older firms, there is a real backlog of scoped cheaper migration projects being unlocked by AI surprisingly fast", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116526543346483419"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-10-31T11:44:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116496495864390037"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 166, "start": 162, "tag": "QPR"}, {"end": 173, "start": 167, "tag": "QPRFC"}, {"end": 184, "start": 174, "tag": "SaintsQPR"}, {"end": 198, "start": 185, "tag": "Championship"}], "mentions": [{"end": 203, "id": "71210107", "start": 199, "username": "QPR"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/wGE0eISXQj", "end": 227, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116496495864390037/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116496