end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116485855594377465/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116485852469571584", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/WDDpuJlfcX"}]}, "id": "2116485855594377465", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 37, "impression_count": 28344, "like_count": 261, "quote_count": 9, "reply_count": 37, "retweet_count": 67}, "text": "From the WSJ, and further to earlier posts:\n\"For years, the companies behind America’s artificial-intelligence boom have raised hundreds of billions of dollars with ease. Wall Street eagerly ponied up capital and asked few questions.\nNow, the balance of power is shifting.\nLenders https://t.co/WDDpuJlfcX", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2116485855594377465"}, {"author_id": "25098482", "created_at": "2026-10-31T10:00:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116470406202999287"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Emerging markets’ growing economic clout is not matched by their influence in global governance", "display_url": "imf.org/en/publication…", "end": 197, "expanded_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/publications/fandd/issues/2026/09/book-review-the-rise-of-emerged-markets-mahmood-pradhan", "images": [{"height": 1077, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114386718354964480/Uw8YL5GF?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 2656}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2114386718354964480/Uw8YL5GF?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 174, "status": 200, "title": "The Rise of ‘Emerged’ Markets", "unwound_url": "https://www.imf.org/en/publications/fandd/issues/2026/09/book-review-the-rise-of-emerged-markets-mahmood-pradhan", "url": "https://t.co/SbPd8JiYQS"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/d0H17JjaY1", "end": 221, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2116470406202999287/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116470247360540672", "start": 198, "url": "https://t.co/d0H17JjaY1"}]}, "id": "2116470406202999287", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 9, "impression_count": 17305, "like_count": 51, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 20}, "text": "Emerging markets now account for more than a third of global GDP, yet their influence in global institutions has yet to catch up, Mahmood Pradhan writes in F&amp;D magazine. https://t.co/SbPd8JiYQS https://t.co/d0H17JjaY1", "url": "https://x.com/IMFNews/status/2116470406202999287"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-31T00:56:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116333409760927780"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/QX3LLWmlb6", "end": 27, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116333409760927780/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116333357822824448", "start": 4, "url": "https://t.co/QX3LLWmlb6"}, {"display_url": "x.com/hugo_edwards_/…", "end": 51, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/hugo_edwards_/status/2116262738225955120", "start": 28, "url": "https://t.co/KLbJIydCu9"}]}, "id": "2116333409760927780", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 90, "impression_count": 54711, "like_count": 461, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 27, "retweet_count": 25}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116262738225955120", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Huh https://t.co/QX3LLWmlb6 https://t.co/KLbJIydCu9", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116333409760927780"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-10-31T00:07:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116321075164500438"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/nickbaumann_/s…", "end": 307, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/nickbaumann_/status/2116302459358572942", "start": 284, "url": "https://t.co/7ikXeBxhWH"}]}, "id": "2116321075164500438", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 436, "impression_count": 49779, "like_count": 456, "quote_count": 11, "reply_count": 211, "retweet_count": 13}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2116302459358572942", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "This is some good advice on working with a Dot (I will never stop capitalizing it, OpenAI!) but also a sign of the issues with the UX of Dot (&amp; all personal agents) right now: you can't easily tell what they are working on, what they know about you, and what they will do for you https://t.co/7ikXeBxhWH", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2116321075164500438"}, {"author_id": "612896910", "created_at": "2026-10-30T22:29:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116296512418267476"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 70, "start": 62, "tag": "BLSdata"}, {"end": 81, "start": 71, "tag": "Halloween"}], "urls": [{"description": "The .gov means it's official. Federal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you're on a federal government site. The site is secure. The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely. Natalie Ho is an economist in the Office of Prices and Living Conditions, U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics. Candy, often considered an everyday luxury, has gotten more expensive", "display_url": "bls.gov/opub/mlr/2026/…", "end": 61, "expanded_url": "https://www.bls.gov/opub/mlr/2026/article/why-is-candy-so-expensive-these-days.htm", "images": [{"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116296559839064064/h77PEmue?format=png&name=orig", "width": 228}, {"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2116296559839064064/h77PEmue?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 126}], "start": 38, "status": 200, "title": "Why is candy so expensive these days? : Monthly Labor Review : U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics", "unwound_url": "https://www.bls.gov/opub/mlr/2026/article/why-is-candy-so-expensive-these-days.htm", "url": "https://t.co/R0EMq77r2P"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/xfytYOhpXm", "end": 105, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2116296512418267476/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2116296275373023232", "start": 82, "url": "https://t.co/xfytYOhpXm"}]}, "id": "2116296512418267476", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2506, "like_coun